WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.840
- Hey guys, welcome to another episode

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.070
of the Wednesday Checkup.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.670
There's a ton of confusion
and even some misinformation

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.560
out there about antibody tests.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.110
So I thought I'd set the record straight.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.790
I'll give you the scoop on what happens

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.480
when you're infected with COVID-19,

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.960
how your immune system reacts,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.160
and what's the deal with
all these antibody tests.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.590
Should you be running out to get one?

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.300
I'll answer those questions
and more starting now.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.960
(rhythmic instrumental music)

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.710
First things first, let's
talk about what happens

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.440
if you're infected with COVID-19.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.840
Well first, you have to be exposed

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.690
to someone who has COVID-19.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.430
Generally, that person will either cough

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.870
or sneeze and expel respiratory droplets

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.590
that then have to make contact
with your mucous membranes,

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.800
your mouth, your nose, your eyes.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.430
Sometimes they'll land on your hand

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.000
and then you'll make
contact with your face.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.700
Then, one of those viral particles

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.750
will attach itself to one of your cells.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.200
It will then make its way inside the cell

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.800
and actually start making copies of itself

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.890
using your own cellular machinery,

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.190
much like a Xerox machine.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.180
Those infected particles
will start spreading

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.210
throughout your body,
mostly through the upper

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.270
and lower airways, that's
where COVID-19 seems to thrive.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.520
That's when your immune
system kicks into high gear

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.350
and starts kicking that virus's butt.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.630
However, at the same time,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.950
your immune system
starts making antibodies.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.520
That's a protein substance
which actually gives you

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.560
lasting immunity against the virus.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.330
Let's take chicken pox as an example.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.810
If you were to get the virus
that causes chicken pox,

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.590
your body fights it off, clears it,

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.320
and then it creates these antibodies,

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.220
which serve as a lasting immunity.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.540
Generally speaking,
chicken pox is an illness

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.070
that you get only once in your life

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.350
because of these antibodies.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.720
Now let's move on and talk about

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.440
the testing for these antibodies.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.340
Generally there are two types of tests,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.840
qualitative and quantitative.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.710
Qualitative tests simply
give us a yes or no answer,

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.020
whether there's a presence
of antibodies at all.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.250
For example, if you've
ever had a strep swab

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.950
or a nasal flu swab, those
are qualitative tests,

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.230
positive or negative only.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:50.710
Quantitative tests give
us a numerical value

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.970
which establishes how many
antibodies are existing

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:54.870
in our blood.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.640
These are generally higher-end tests

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.490
that we actually have to send out to a lab

00:01:58.490 --> 00:01:59.400
through a blood sample.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.990
Let's summarize what we know now.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.660
You get an infection with COVID-19,

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.800
your immune system kicks
its butt, clears it,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.130
creates a lasting immunity
through a protein substance

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.410
known as an antibody.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.980
We can test for this antibody.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.630
So shouldn't we give this test
to as many people as possible

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.470
so we can send them
out into the work force

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:15.560
because they're protected?

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.400
Not so fast.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.530
There's actually three problems
with these antibody tests

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.630
I'm about to let you know about.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.410
Problem number one is we
simply don't have enough

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.170
information on what to do with
the results of these tests.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.640
For example, let's say you go out

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.800
and get a qualitative test
and you get a positive result.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.680
All that really tells us is
that you've had COVID-19.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.460
It doesn't quite tell us
about your level of immunity.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.810
'Cause perhaps you had a really mild case

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:40.200
and your immune system didn't
build up enough antibodies

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.500
to protect you for the next time.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.280
So the solution might be,
let's get a quantitative test.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.850
Well that's better and you're
gonna get a numerical value

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.850
telling us how many
antibodies are present.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.740
However, we then need to
rely on reference ranges.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.020
Let me explain reference ranges.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.660
If you've ever gotten a test to see

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.680
if you're immune to measles,
you get a numerical value back.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.020
And then we look at
reference ranges to see

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.810
if it's above this value then
you know the person's immune.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.670
If it falls in between these two numbers,

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:05.680
their immunity is falling

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.560
and they likely need another booster shot.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.800
And if it's below this value,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.930
they're definitely not immune

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.550
and they should get a booster asap.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.920
With COVID-19, whatever
number we get is great,

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:15.830
it might be accurate.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.040
But we don't have these
reference ranges set up

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.310
like we do with measles

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.710
of which we have decades
worth of research.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.270
COVID-19 is a novel virus.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.500
These reference ranges
take years to develop.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.940
So it's gonna take some time
until we know what's what.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:30.800
And the final point of all this

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.910
is we don't know how
long the immunity lasts.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.760
Perhaps you do have antibodies,
perhaps you are immune.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.590
But how long's that immunity gonna last?

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.290
Is it gonna be one week, one
month, one year or a lifetime?

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.790
We don't know that information
yet, but we will soon.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:46.220
The second problem here
is poor quality tests.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.610
There's over a hundred of
these tests on the market

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:52.240
with only four of them being
FDA approved through an EUA,

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.490
that's the Emergency Use Authorization.

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:57.140
It essentially allows
companies with limited evidence

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.410
but still decent evidence
to show at the FDA

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.970
their product actually worked.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.980
Think about the dozens that are out there,

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:06.090
that are really poor quality,
manufactured god knows where,

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.820
and could be giving questionable results.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.720
Problem number three,
the false positive rate.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.380
Look, no test is perfect.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.040
They all have a margin of error.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.730
And one of the examples of
that is the false positive rate

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.860
where it tells you you're
positive, but you're actually not.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.070
It's flat out wrong.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.500
And some of the best tests
have a 5% false positive rate.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.700
That sounds pretty good,

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.730
but let's take this
example into consideration.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.400
Picture yourself in a town of 100 people,

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.940
and five of those people have
had COVID-19 and cleared it.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.420
And the government wants
to use this antibody test

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.210
to find out who those five people are.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.550
There gonna give the test to everybody

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.350
and they're gonna find out
five people have had it.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.050
But because it has a
5% false positive rate,

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.050
five other individuals
will also test positive

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.070
even though they've never had COVID-19.

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:51.330
That makes for a total
of 10 positive tests,

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.820
five of which are accurate.

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.720
That means a 50% accuracy, not so accurate

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:58.130
because the prevalence of
the disease is quite low.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.350
But when the prevalence
of the disease goes up,

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:03.150
say, 50 people have had it in this town.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.480
You have 50 people test
positive correctly,

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.890
five people test positive incorrectly,

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:11.330
and when you do the math,
it's at over 90% accuracy.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.860
You see how the prevalence of an illness

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.450
can affect the accuracy of a test?

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.750
That false positive rate

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.060
really needs to be
taken into consideration

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.330
when we use it in areas

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.900
with a low prevalence of COVID-19.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.720
All that goes to show

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.190
that you as an individual
should not run out

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.690
to get tested for COVID-19 antibodies.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.640
We just don't yet know what
to do with the information.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.680
We can't tell you if you're 100% immune

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.150
even if you do test positive.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.700
The last thing we want you to do

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.630
is think you have a layer of
security when you truly do not.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:43.150
What we can use this
information for is on a state,

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:46.930
on a government level to see
where COVID-19 is prevalent.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.640
How many people have had
COVID-19 and not even known it?

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.060
What's the true fatality
rate of this virus?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.090
And which areas can we start loosening

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.820
the social restrictions in
to get our economy back.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.970
This antibody test is really important.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:01.090
But it's not important
to us as individuals.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.340
It's important to us as a whole nation.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.830
Please, if you have any questions

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.200
about these antibody tests,
leave 'em down below.

